YARA-L catalogs (catalogs/yaral/).

udm.toml and functions.toml are generated by scripts/sync_yaral_catalogs.py
from Google Security Operations documentation, Copyright Google LLC, licensed
under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 License
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/):

- the Unified Data Model field list
  (https://cloud.google.com/chronicle/docs/reference/udm-field-list);
- the Chronicle API `Collection` resource
  (https://cloud.google.com/chronicle/docs/reference/rest/v1alpha/Collection);
- the YARA-L 2.0 functions page
  (https://cloud.google.com/chronicle/docs/yara-l/functions);
- the metrics functions page
  (https://cloud.google.com/chronicle/docs/detection/metrics-functions);
- the outcome syntax page and the search statistics page, for the outcome
  aggregations.

Message, field, enum and function names, types, labels and availability are
reformatted as TOML; each field's and function's first sentence is copied, as
published, for hover. Changes: tables flattened into rows, camelCase API
field names written in snake_case as YARA-L reads them.
